# Art handoff (overrides)

On 2026-10-21 Nathan moved all remaining art and animation work from Pixel (Grok Bot) to his Cursor project. Pixel no longer draws, wires, reviews, or answers art requests.

Before any art, animation, UI, or `assets/**` work, read `design/handoff/CURSOR-AGENT/README.md` and `design/handoff/CURSOR-AGENT/TASK.md`. They hold Pixel's rules, specs, build order, and PixelLab workflow. Specs live in `design/handoff/CURSOR-AGENT/specs/` and `design/visual/`.

Where `swipe-design-loop.mdc`, `unique-art.mdc`, or `corrupt-png.mdc` say "Pixel draws / owns PNG bytes / supplies art", read it as: the Cursor art agent makes the art with PixelLab, following the handoff README. Specifically:
- You may create and replace PNGs, but only through PixelLab (`design/handoff/CURSOR-AGENT/pixellab/`, token from env `PIXELLAB_API_TOKEN`) plus grid/palette cleanup. Hand-fix only small issues, or a piece PixelLab failed twice.
- Crypt Classic style: 1px #100e0c outline, light from upper-left, no anti-aliasing, gold #FFD84A, palette in `design/handoff/CURSOR-AGENT/palette/`, Nearest filter, lossless, no mipmaps.
- One contact sheet per batch, attached to the PR for Nathan.
- You may wire new ids into `ITEM_PNG` / `MONSTER_PNG`.
- ART-REQUEST sections are now work for the Cursor project, not Pixel. `tools\request_art.cmd` pings a paused Grok Bot routine and does nothing useful.
- Per handoff pass: branch, PR, local QA on Cherry (`LOCAL-QA-PROMPT.md`), then merge to main. This replaces "no merges, no pushes" for handoff work only.

Unchanged and still hard rules: never edit player-facing copy (Jam owns `data/player-copy.json`; flag it in the PR). Never show "Tier", "ATK", or "atk" to players. Normal animation speed is 0.675; Shift fast-forward is 2.025. Never touch Nathan's `movement` checkout or its uncommitted work. Never kill a Godot process you didn't start. Never export or push to itch. Never commit secrets.
